List what is published and why, or choose what to publish.

\e[1mUsage\e[0m: \e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mselect\e[0m \e[36m[OPTIONS]\e[0m \e[36m[PATHS]...\e[0m

\e[1mExamples\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mselect\e[0m                \e[2m# \e[0mList every page, whether it is published, and why
  \e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mselect\e[0m notes/trip.md  \e[2m# \e[0mPublish one page of a vault

\e[1mArguments\e[0m
  \e[36m[PATHS]...\e[0m  Pages to select, as paths in the folder: `\e[1m\e[36mpublish:\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mtrue\e[0m` is
              written into the frontmatter of each, which the file must already
              have. Without a path or `\e[1m\e[36m--folder\e[0m`, every page is listed with
              whether it is published and why

\e[1mOptions\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --folder\e[0m \e[36m<GLOB>\e[0m  Select every file a glob matches (`\e[1m\e[36mnotes/**\e[0m`) by adding
                       it to `\e[1m\e[36minclude\e[0m` in ink.toml
  \e[1m\e[36m    --remove\e[0m         Take the selection back: remove `\e[1m\e[36mpublish:\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mtrue\e[0m` from each
                       page, or the glob from `\e[1m\e[36minclude\e[0m`. In a public source a
                       page that is not selected is still published by default
  \e[1m\e[36m    --dry-run\e[0m        Say what would be written and write nothing

\e[1mExit codes\e[0m
  0  Done; warnings, if any, were printed
  1  The site has errors
  2  Wrong usage, or a folder that is missing; nothing was changed

\e[2mSee also\e[0m  \e[1m\e[36mink explain\e[0m, \e[1m\e[36mink pin\e[0m
\e[2mDocs\e[0m      \e[4m\e[36mhttps://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md\e[0m
